        "original_id": "808f481c-3d44-5947-ba0c-a49c0fe3f4b9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1981 CART PPG Indy Car World Series season\n- People: Rick Mears\n- Places: Avondale, Arizona; Wichita, Kansas\n- Topics: U.S. open-wheel racing\n\nFacts:\n- Rick Mears was born on December 3, 1951, in Wichita, Kansas.\n- Rick Mears, nicknamed \"Rocket Rick,\" is a retired American race car driver.\n- The 1981 CART PPG Indy Car World Series season was the third season in the CART era of U.S. open-wheel racing.\n- The 1981 CART PPG Indy Car World Series season consisted of 11 races.\n- The 1981 CART PPG Indy Car World Series season began in Avondale, Arizona on March 22, 1981, and concluded there on October 31, 1981.\n- Rick Mears was the Drivers' Champion of the 1981 PPG Indy Car World Series.",
